	There's a huge difference. Gas spores explode when and *only*
when killed, while spheres explode as an active attack, and *don't*
explode when killed. This is readily observable, in that smacking down a
sphere that's right next to you doesn't hurt, while doing it to a gas
spore does, and that gas spores will follow you around without exploding
as long as you don't hit them, while spheres explode immediately when
they get next to you even if you don't hit them.

	There are obvious implications for the tactics of dealing with
each here. Gas spores need to be treated much like floating eyes, killed
with ranged attacks at a distance (the "distance" part is important,
unlike for eyes), and can be pretty safely ignored as long as you're
careful not to bump into them or let them corner you. Spheres, on the
other hand, need to be dropped by the fastest means available as soon as
they show up, and melee is not excluded as your last line of defense.

